Article 1 – Purpose

Guildy is a Minecraft mod created by NightFury (“the Author”). This license sets
out what you may do with Guildy. Anything it does not expressly allow is
forbidden without the Author's written permission.


Article 2 – Acceptance

Downloading, installing, using, modifying or distributing Guildy, in whole or in
part, means that you accept this license. If you do not accept it, you may not
use Guildy.


Article 3 – Definitions

“Guildy”: the mod, in all its versions and with all its elements, including its
source code and compiled files, its drawings, textures, icons and models, its
builds (ruins, structures, buildings, schematics), its texts, names and content,
its guide and documentation, its resource pack and its default configuration
files.

“Official version”: a file of Guildy published by the Author, without any
modification.

“Official page”: the repository https://github.com/softpython2884/Guildy and the
Guildy pages published by the Author, in particular on CurseForge and Modrinth.

“Public server”: a server open to players other than its operator and their
private circle, in particular if it is publicly advertised (server list,
website, social network, open Discord server).

“Monetized server”: a server that asks for or receives money, or anything else
of value, in connection with the server: paid access or whitelist, ranks, perks,
items, cosmetics, in-game currency, subscriptions, donations, advertising, paid
partnerships. Members of a private server sharing its hosting costs, with
nothing in return in game, is not monetization.


Article 4 – Ownership

Guildy is a work protected by copyright. Its elements, including its drawings,
textures, models and builds, are original creations of the Author, except for
the third-party elements listed in article 11. The Author keeps all of their
rights: this license grants permissions to use Guildy, it does not transfer any
right.


Article 5 – What you may do

Provided that you comply with this license, you may:

1. Download an official version, install and use it, in particular on your
   Minecraft servers, private or public, and play on them.
2. Host Guildy's official resource pack and send it to the players of your
   server, for use on that server.
3. Change the configuration files provided by Guildy and share those files. This
   is not a modification of Guildy within the meaning of this license.
4. Read and study Guildy's code, compile it and modify it for your own use,
   including running your modified version on your servers, without ever
   distributing it.
5. Include an official version in a modpack, under the conditions of article 7.
6. Show Guildy in videos, live streams, screenshots, articles or guides,
   including monetized ones, as long as you do not present it as your creation.
7. Fork the repository on GitHub, within GitHub's Terms of Service, to propose
   contributions to the Author.
8. Use the name “Guildy” to state that your server or modpack uses it, or to
   talk about it.

These permissions are free of charge, worldwide and for the whole term of
copyright protection, unless terminated (article 13). They are non-exclusive and
non-transferable.


Article 6 – What is forbidden

Unless the Author gives written permission, you may not:

1. Sell or rent Guildy, charge for downloading or accessing it, or sublicense
   it.
2. Distribute a modified version of Guildy in any form (compiled file, source
   code, patch), or a project that reuses its code.
3. Distribute Guildy outside the cases provided for in article 5: republish it,
   upload it to another website or platform, mirror it or share a copy of it.
4. Reuse elements of Guildy outside Guildy, in particular its drawings,
   textures, models, builds and texts, in another mod, a resource pack, a map, a
   server or any other project.
5. Appropriate Guildy: present it as your creation, remove or alter the author,
   license or credit notices, claim any right over Guildy or any of its
   elements, or register in your name a trademark, a domain name or any other
   title using the name “Guildy”.
6. Use the name “Guildy” for another project, or in a way that suggests that the
   Author supports or endorses your project.
7. Run Guildy on a monetized server without the permission required by
   article 8.


Article 7 – Modpacks

You may include Guildy in a modpack if all of these conditions are met:

1. The modpack contains an official, unmodified version. It may ship its own
   configuration files.
2. The modpack is free: neither downloading it nor accessing it is paid. The
   rewards a platform pays its creators out of its own revenue, such as
   CurseForge or Modrinth, do not make a modpack paid.
3. The modpack's page or description credits Guildy and its author, with a link
   to the official page, for example: “Guildy, a mod by NightFury: <link>”.
4. The modpack does not present Guildy as part of its own content.


Article 8 – Servers

1. A public server that uses Guildy must say so clearly, somewhere its players
   can see it: in its public presentation (website, server list page, Discord
   server or server description). The notice names Guildy and its author and
   links to the official page, for example: “This server uses Guildy, a mod by
   NightFury: <link>”. If the server runs a modified version, the notice says
   so.
2. A monetized server may only use Guildy with the Author's prior written
   permission, requested by email at contact@forgenet.fr. The Author is free to
   accept or refuse and may set conditions. A permission only applies to the
   server and under the conditions it names.


Article 9 – Contributions

By submitting a contribution to Guildy (pull request, patch, drawing, build or
text), you guarantee that you have the right to do so, and you allow the Author,
free of charge, worldwide and for the whole term of copyright, to use it, modify
it, include it in Guildy and distribute it, under this license or any other
license.


Article 10 – Earlier versions marked MIT

The versions of Guildy published before this license contained a file stating
the MIT license. That notice was a mistake: it was the default template offered
by the code editor, and Guildy was never meant to be distributed under the MIT
license. Guildy is not an MIT-licensed project. To the fullest extent permitted
by law, this license applies to all versions of Guildy, including those that
carried that notice.


Article 11 – Third-party elements

Minecraft and its elements belong to Mojang Studios and Microsoft. Guildy is not
an official Minecraft product: it is not approved by or associated with Mojang
or Microsoft. The libraries included in Guildy (SGUI, fabric-permissions-api)
remain under their own licenses. This license does not cover those elements.


Article 12 – No warranty

Guildy is provided “as is”, without any warranty, in particular as to its
operation, its compatibility or the absence of defects. To the fullest extent
permitted by law, the Author is not liable for any damage, direct or indirect,
arising from the use of Guildy or the inability to use it, including any loss of
data or worlds.


Article 13 – Termination

Any breach of this license automatically ends, without notice, the permissions
it grants you. You must then stop using and distributing Guildy and delete the
copies in your possession. The Author may reinstate those permissions in
writing. Termination does not deprive the Author of any other right or remedy.


Article 14 – Other permissions

Any permission not provided for by this license (sale, distribution,
monetization, reuse of elements, etc.) must be requested by email at
contact@forgenet.fr. Only a written permission from the Author binds them.


Article 15 – Changes to this license

The Author may publish new versions of this license. A new version applies to
the versions of Guildy published after it.


Article 16 – Governing law

This license is governed by French law. If any of its clauses is held void or
unenforceable, the others remain in force.
